# The player's own save (money, fleet, routes in progress). Written by
# SaveGame at runtime - it's per-player state, not project data, so it must
# not travel with the repo the way the layout files under game/data/ do.
#
# THE REPO CARRIES A DAY 0 SAVE, and these are how it stays one. All four are
# written by SaveGame as you play; absent, the game starts fresh, which is
# exactly what a clone should do. They were merely untracked before, so a
# `git add -A` would have published a live playthrough over the baseline.
game/data/player.json
game/data/apron_progress.json
game/data/building_progress.json
game/data/zone_progress.json
game/data/apron_skins_owned.json
